# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Pages' default for everything is `public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate`.
# Four hours of browser-side caching is fine for artwork and wrong for code:
# it means a deploy does not necessarily reach a phone that loaded the site
# earlier that morning, which on 12-13 September is the difference between
# shipping a fix and thinking you shipped a fix.
#
# `no-cache` does not mean "do not cache". It means "cache it, then revalidate
# before every reuse" - so a reload costs one conditional request and gets a
# 304 with no body whenever nothing changed. That is the right trade for the
# handful of files listed here.
#
# Artwork and fonts deliberately keep the default. They are cache-first inside
# the service worker, which only refetches them when VERSION moves, and that
# refetch bypasses the HTTP cache (see `fresh` in sw.js). Putting them on
# no-cache would add a revalidation round-trip per crest per load for no gain,
# on a weekend whose egress budget is the reason for the Supabase Pro upgrade.

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
